    <!--
        Sheep (S5, 2026-10-13; sources reviewed 2026-10-14). The species stays off until the weight
        model's SHEEP type is enabled. Each value is a sourced figure, a model approximation of a
        table, a PROXY or a calibration value; tests/sheepcalib.py reports each against its table.
        AHDB "Feeding the ewe" (older edition, AFRC 1993 tables):
        - maintenanceMEPerKgMetabolic 0.37: model approximation. AHDB puts maintenance at about 12%
          of live weight in MJ ME (70 kg: 8.4 housed, about 9 outdoors) = 0.35-0.37 per kg^0.75.
          Against Table 29 extrapolated to no milk the model is 5-6% high.
        - pregnancyFactor 0.55 a lamb x maintenance, rising linearly over the last 40% of the
          pregnancy (pregnancyRampStart 0.6): model approximation of Table 8 (70 kg, one week
          before lambing: single 14.4, twins 18.3 MJ). Over Table 8's cells singles and twins are
          within -8%..+0%. physiology pregnancyThirdLambFactor 0.50: a third lamb (and any
          further) costs half of one of the first two - Table 8's own 70 kg row, where the
          triplet - twin increment is 0.47-0.52 of the twin - single one at 7/5/3/1 weeks (mean
          0.50); the 80 kg row (0.48-0.55) is held out to check it. Without it triplets were up
          to +11% (a linear count overstates the third lamb).
        - milk meMJPerKg 8.3: the slope of Table 29 (housed ewes, 11.5 MJ/kg DM diet), an
          approximation for those diets, not a constant across diets. Table 29's 18 cells are within
          +2%..+6% of maintenance + 8.3 x milk - 35 x loss.
        - reserveMobilizeMEPerKg 35 (Table 29: 50 g a day lost saves about 1.75 MJ) and
          reserveDepositMEPerKg 50 (Table 8 note: 50 g a day gained costs 2.5 MJ).
        - intake: Table 2 (dry 1.5%, late pregnancy 2-2.5%, lactation 3-3.5% of live weight).
        - lactation (nursing): Table 28, a ewe's monthly mean milk (kg a day) in months 1-3 by
          system and lambs suckled; one step a month, so each month's integral is the table's
          (AFRC has hill and lowland only; a triplet's dam is held at the twin row).
        Lambs: youngMaintenanceMEPerKgMetabolic 0.475, a candidate between the Awassi lamb trial's
        0.466 and 0.482 (C-grade summary); using it to 6 months and moving to the ewe's 0.37 by 12
        is a model assumption.
        Growth: growthMEPerKgAt500 33 at growthReferenceKg 40 (linear in weight, floor 14) and the
        sex factors growthCostMale / Castrate / Female 0.80 / 1.00 / 1.25 are calibration values
        (set on routes R1 / R4 and the trial's ADG ratio, SHEEP-C11), not verified physiology.
        damMilk dm 0.19, me 25, cp 0.28: PROXY. Sebek and Everts 1993 give GE = 41.94 fat + 15.85
        protein + 21.41 lactose kJ/kg (ranges 44-125, 32-53, 39-53 g/kg); a typical meat ewe's milk
        (75, 53, 48 g/kg) is about 5.013 MJ GE a kg as drunk, 19% DM, CP 28% of DM. ME 25 MJ/kg DM
        (4.75 a kg as drunk) assumes ME/GE 0.9475: no source gives it (AHDB p50: about 6.5 MJ ME
        from milk a twin lamb at six weeks is consistent). The calibration reports the routes at
        other values.
        Concentrate adaptation 14 days (Teagasc: ad lib in 10 days; SRUC 2-3 weeks); an unadapted
        lamb may eat up to 50% concentrate in its DM - a game rule (FAS's 50% is barley within the
        concentrate mix). Creep 0.35 kg DM a day (about 0.4 kg fresh, range 0.3-0.5). Weaning at 3
        months (AHDB: wean at 12 weeks, 90 days; lambs are not drinking significant milk by then);
        an orphan from 2 months with 250 g of creep a day as fed (fresh weight, converted by each
        feed's DM; 0.22 kg DM only for a feed of about 88% DM) for 3.5 model days in a row (AHDB
        lambing ewe lambs: 8-9 weeks, 250 g/day for 3-4 days; 3.5 is the range's midpoint).
    -->
    <species name="SHEEP">
        <requirements maintenanceMEPerKgMetabolic="0.37" growthMEPerKgAt500="33" growthWeightExponent="1.0" growthMEPerKgMin="14"
            reserveDepositMEPerKg="50" reserveMobilizeMEPerKg="35" catabolismMEPerKg="10" pregnancyFactor="0.55"/>
        <physiology growthReferenceKg="40" youngMaintenanceMEPerKgMetabolic="0.475" youngMaintenanceUntilMonth="6"
            adultMaintenanceFromMonth="12" calfGrowthCost="0"
            growthCostMale="0.80" growthCostCastrate="1.0" growthCostFemale="1.25" pregnancyThirdLambFactor="0.50"/>
        <calf maintenanceMEPerKgMetabolic="0.37"/>
        <intake growingPerKgMetabolic="0.092" dryPerKgMetabolic="0.060" lactatingPerKgMetabolic="0.050"
            lactatingPerKgMilk="0.50" calfSolidPerKgMetabolic="0.095"
            ndfFillGrowing="0.018" ndfFillDry="0.012" ndfFillLactating="0.018" ndfFillCalf="0.016"/>
        <protein maintenance="0.07" calf="0.18" young="0.15" growing="0.13" finishing="0.12"
