    <!--
        Pigs (pig P5, 2026-10-16; FS25_PigBreeds_离线准备_2026-10-16/PIG_P5_单胃营养设计.md, p5_derive.py). Growing pigs on
        NRC (2012) Nutrient Requirements of Swine, chapter 8 (growing-finishing model); the species stays off until the
        weight model's PIG type is enabled (it stays off). No rumen: monogastric (RLFeedRationPlanner.planMonogastric).
        - maintenanceMEPerKgMetabolic 0.8243 MJ per kg^0.60 (monogastric maintenanceExponent 0.60): 197 kcal ME x BW^0.60
          (Eq. 8-19).
        - Frame (everything but body lipid): its protein share from Eqs. 8-2, 8-3 and 8-5 (water and ash on body protein,
          gut fill) x 10.6 kcal ME a g of protein deposited (Eq. 8-31; Tess et al. 1984): 7.0 MJ/kg at 5 kg to 11.2 at
          150 kg, as growthMEPerKgAt500 10.03 at growthReferenceKg 60 x (W / 60)^0.133 (largest error 1.6% at 7-135 kg),
          at least 7.0.
        - Reserve = body lipid: 12.5 kcal ME a g laid down (52.3 MJ/kg); mobilised at an energetic efficiency of 0.80 of
          its 9.4 kcal/g (31.5 MJ/kg; Eq. 8-65 text, ch. 1). Frame given back once the lipid is spent: its protein
          (0.227 of a kg at 60 kg) x 5.6 kcal/g x 0.80 = 4.3 MJ/kg (PROXY: the lipid efficiency applied to protein).
        - Intake eaten freely: ME a day a x (1 - exp(-exp(b) x W^c)), gilts Eq. 8-10, barrows 8-11, entire males 8-12 (3%
          below gilts), within the physical capacity 111 g x W^0.803 a day (Eq. 8-16) at 90% DM. A low-energy ration is
          eaten in more DM up to that capacity ("energy content of the diet controls the amount consumed"). No feed
          wastage (NRC's typical 5%), temperature or stocking density.
        - SID lysine for full growth, g per MJ ME: Table 16-1A (5-135 kg, both sexes) and Table 16-2A from 50 kg by sex,
          each % at its diet ME (3300-3400 kcal/kg, 90% DM) / 4.184; growth falls linearly to nothing at 0.05 g/MJ (the
          gut and skin losses of Eqs. 8-40 to 8-42 at about 60 kg).
        - A pen with a pig under 28 model days (not weaned, design D3), a pregnant female or one that has farrowed keeps
          the old rules (PIG_BREEDING_LEGACY): the sow's milk, pregnancy and body condition are P6/P7. Its covered pigs'
          weight still follows their own curve there (RLFeed.stepFallback: the budget pays their needs x the pen's food
          factor), never the old fixed gain; an approximation until the sow's milk and litter budget exist.
        - Feeds: INRA-CIRAD-AFZ tables (feedtables.com) and Feedipedia, read 2026-10-16, pig ME and SID lysine on DM;
          density the engine's massPerLiter (Hof Bergmann 1.5b1). A pig eats every feed in its trough it may, mixed as
          stocked (a mixed trough), each at most its maxShare; PIGLETFOOD only up to 25 kg.
    -->
